                    "authorAssociation": "NONE",
                    "body": "That's correct. `vim.o.list` is `false` and `vim.o.listchars` contains `tab:>`.\r\n\r\n<img width=\"405\" height=\"107\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/c012de45-9c21-4c45-919b-ed0c6b8ceabc\" />\r\n\r\nYour explanation makes sense. Since this behavior is inconsistent with mini.files , should I consider this a bug to be patched in the future? For now I added the following code before the plugin setup and it solved the problem:\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nvim.o.listchars = \"tab:  ,trail:-,nbsp:+\"\r\n```",
                    "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">That's correct. <code class=\"notranslate\">vim.o.list</code> is <code class=\"notranslate\">false</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">vim.o.listchars</code> contains <code class=\"notranslate\">tab:&gt;</code>.</p>\n<a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/35900428/536381834-c012de45-9c21-4c45-919b-ed0c6b8ceabc.png?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..8l8hMxO07ji5ZUVPDtFktki_O9dMVsRph0-F59yGNqE\"><img width=\"405\" height=\"107\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/35900428/536381834-c012de45-9c21-4c45-919b-ed0c6b8ceabc.png?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..8l8hMxO07ji5ZUVPDtFktki_O9dMVsRph0-F59yGNqE\" style=\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; max-height: 107px;; aspect-ratio: 405 / 107; background-color: var(--bgColor-muted); border-radius: 6px\" class=\"js-gh-image-fallback\"></a>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Your explanation makes sense. Since this behavior is inconsistent with mini.files , should I consider this a bug to be patched in the future? For now I added the following code before the plugin setup and it solved the problem:</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-lua notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"vim.o.listchars = &quot;tab:  ,trail:-,nbsp:+&quot;\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">o</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">listchars</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>tab:  ,trail:-,nbsp:+<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span></pre></div>",
                    "bodyText": "That's correct. vim.o.list is false and vim.o.listchars contains tab:>.\n\nYour explanation makes sense. Since this behavior is inconsistent with mini.files , should I consider this a bug to be patched in the future? For now I added the following code before the plugin setup and it solved the problem:\nvim.o.listchars = \"tab:  ,trail:-,nbsp:+\"",
